{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal fails to meet the minimum original floor area required to be eligible for conversion to a HMO and is not located a suitable location for a HMO, due to the distance to the town centre facilities and insufficient access to public transport. The proposal is therefore unacceptable in principle, contrary to Local Plan Policy SC10 and the Council's Houses in Multiple Occupation SPD.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed roof extension, as a result of its excessive size and scale and inappropriate design, represent bulky, obtrusive and incongruous addition which would be disproportionate to the host property and would harm the character and appearance of the wider area. Thus, making it contrary to adopted Local Plan Policies CC1, CC2 and SC7 and the intent of the Hounslow Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD (2024).",
    "Reason : 3 - The applicant has failed to demonstrate that the proposal would not result in an unacceptable highways impact to the detriment of highway and pedestrian safety. The proposed development is therefore contrary to Local Plan Policy EC2, London Plan Policy T5 and the LBH Residential Crossovers and Off-Street Parking Policy (2016). "
  ],
